{"name":"Deep Thoughts","hex":"#728787","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deep","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extending, reaching or positioned far from a point of reference, especially downwards.\nExtending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively.","Extending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Far, especially far down through something or into something, physically or figuratively.","In a profound, not superficial, manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep"},{"term":"thoughts","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of thought"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thoughts"}],"entries":[{"title":"List of The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy characters","blocks":[{"text":"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy is a comedy science fiction franchise created by Douglas Adams. Originally a 1978 radio comedy, it was later adapted to other formats, including novels, stage shows, comic books, a 1981 TV series, a 1984 text adventure game, and 2005 feature film. The various versions follow the same basic plot. However, in many places, they are mutually contradictory, as Adams rewrote the story substantially for each new adaptation. Throughout all versions, the series follows the adventures of Arthur Dent and his interactions with Ford Prefect, Zaphod Beeblebrox, Marvin the Paranoid Android, and Trillian."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_The_Hitchhiker's_Guide_to_the_Galaxy_characters"},{"title":"Deep Thought (chess computer)","blocks":[{"text":"Deep Thought was a computer designed to play chess. Deep Thought was initially developed at Carnegie Mellon University and later at IBM. It was second in the line of chess computers developed by Feng-hsiung Hsu, starting with ChipTest and culminating in Deep Blue. In addition to Hsu, the Deep Thought team included Thomas Anantharaman, Mike Browne, Murray Campbell and Andreas Nowatzyk. Deep Thought became the first computer to beat a grandmaster in a regular tournament game when it beat Bent Larsen in 1988, but was easily defeated in both games of a two-game match with Garry Kasparov in 1989 as well as in a correspondence match with Michael Valvo."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_Thought_(chess_computer)"},{"title":"Deep Thoughts (Lil Durk album)","blocks":[{"text":"Deep Thoughts is the ninth studio album by American rapper Lil Durk, released through Only the Family (OTF), Alamo Records, and Sony Music on March 28, 2025. The album features guest appearances from Future, Lil Baby, Hunxho, and Jhené Aiko. Production was handled by a variety of producers, including Southside, Chopsquad DJ, Metro Boomin, Lil Yachty, and Benny Blanco, among others. Deep Thoughts serves as the follow-up to Durk's previous album, Almost Healed, and his collaborative studio album with OTF, Nightmares in the Trenches (2023). The album was originally supposed to be released on October 18, 2024, but has since been delayed four times due to his October 2024 arrest on murder-for-hire charges."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2c/Deep_Thoughts_%28Lil_Durk_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_Thoughts_(Lil_Durk_album)"},{"title":"Thought","blocks":[{"text":"Thought, or thinking, is a cognitive process in which the mind considers, creates, or manipulates ideas, representations, or information. Core forms include judging, reasoning, concept formation, problem solving, and deliberation. Other processes, such as entertaining an idea, memory, or imagination, are also frequently considered types of thought. Thought may arise in response to perception, but can also occur without immediate input from the sensory organs. In a broader sense, any mental event—including perception and unconscious processes—may be described as forms of thought. The term can also denote not the process itself, but the resulting mental states or systems of ideas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Jardin_du_Musee_Rodin_Paris_Le_Penseur_20050402_%2802%29.jpg/330px-Jardin_du_Musee_Rodin_Paris_Le_Penseur_20050402_%2802%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thought"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d8/God_%28Non-Existance_of%29.jpg/330px-God_%28Non-Existance_of%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d8/God_%28Non-Existance_of%29.jpg/330px-God_%28Non-Existance_of%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"God, about to disappear in a puff of logic, from HitchHiker's TV series","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGod_(Non-Existance_of).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Hotblack_Desiato_estate_agents_-_February_16_2005.jpg/500px-Hotblack_Desiato_estate_agents_-_February_16_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Hotblack_Desiato_estate_agents_-_February_16_2005.jpg/1280px-Hotblack_Desiato_estate_agents_-_February_16_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Hotblack_Desiato_estate_agents_-_February_16_2005.jpg/500px-Hotblack_Desiato_estate_agents_-_February_16_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A branch of Hotblack Desiato estate agents, after which the character was named, at Camden Town","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHotblack_Desiato_estate_agents_-_February_16_2005.jpg"},{"srcset":"